      "math_academy_id": "q-363851",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$  select the correct options in the computations of the matrix $U$ below. From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce the singular values ${\\sigma }_{1}=5\\sqrt{2}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\n\nNow, we compute the $1$st column of $U.$ It is given by:\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${u}_{1}=\\,\\,$ |  | $\\frac{5}{5\\sqrt{2}}$ |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal.\n\nHence, we must find vectors $u=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}]^{T}$ such that ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nChoosing ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ as free variables, the general solution is given by:\n\n|  |  | ${x}_{1}$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} |  |  |\n\nthat we can rewrite as:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3}{x}_{1}-\\frac{5}{3}{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nNext, we orthogonalize ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ using the Gram-Schmidt process to get the corresponding orthogonal vectors ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nLet ${c}_{1}={b}_{1},$ then:\n\n|  |  | {{field-6}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${c}_{2}=\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-7}} |  |  |\n|  |  | $-3$ |  |  |\n\nFinally, normalizing orthogonal vectors ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ we obtain the second and third columns of $U:$   \n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <table cellpadding=\"0\">\n          <tbody>\n            <tr>\n              <td rowspan=\"3\" width=\"40px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"right\">\n                ${u}_{2}=\\,\\,$\n              </td>\n              <td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n              <td width=\"90px\" align=\"center\">\n                {{field-8}}\n              </td>\n              <td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n              <td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n              <td align=\"center\"></td>\n              <td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n              <td align=\"center\"></td>\n              <td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n              <td align=\"center\"></td>\n              <td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-9}}\n              </td>\n              <td align=\"center\"></td>\n              <td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <table cellpadding=\"0\">\n          <tbody>\n            <tr>\n              <td rowspan=\"3\" width=\"40px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"right\">\n                ${u}_{3}=\\,\\,$\n              </td>\n              <td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n              <td width=\"90px\" align=\"center\">\n                $-\\frac{4}{5\\sqrt{2}}$\n              </td>\n              <td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n              <td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n              <td align=\"center\"></td>\n              <td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-10}}\n              </td>\n              <td align=\"center\"></td>\n              <td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n              <td align=\"center\"></td>\n              <td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-11}}\n              </td>\n              <td align=\"center\"></td>\n              <td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>",
